From 5c013d59d3e734d2497f9c33479006fbfeaa3258 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4ffein <c4ffein.work@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:07:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Scotch 7.0.18: catalog entry, skipped, determinism patch
 carried over

Pin the 7.0.18 GitLab archive (sha256 2cbdcf6d...). It compiles pristine
but fails the reproducibility gate: bgraph_bipart_gg.c is unchanged since
7.0.17, so the threaded greedy bipartitioner still seeds its worker PRNGs
from the shared generator mid-draw and ignores SCOTCH_DETERMINISTIC
(`make bump SCOTCH=7.0.18`: 5 distinct partitions over 12 fresh processes
with the `h` strategy at 4 threads; 3 of 5 gate tests fail).

Record it in _SKIPPED_VERSIONS (the shipped pin stays on 7.0.15) and offer
the 7.0.17 behavioral patch, which applies unchanged, as
scotch-7.0.18-bgraph-bipart-gg-determinism.patch. With it the gate passes
3 x 30 fresh runs. No public C function added or removed since 7.0.15
(library.h); test_api_completeness passes on the 7.0.18 build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019ndjvpJnQWCnRoSKg7huQA
