 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+- **Scotch 7.0.18 catalogued but SKIPPED, with the behavioral patch carried
+  over.** 7.0.18 compiles pristine (sha256 pinned) but fails the
+  reproducibility gate like 7.0.16 and 7.0.17: `bgraph_bipart_gg.c` did not
+  change, so the worker-PRNG seeding race and the missing
+  `SCOTCH_DETERMINISTIC` guard are still there (5 distinct partitions over
+  12 fresh processes with the `h` strategy at 4 threads). It is recorded in
+  `_SKIPPED_VERSIONS`, the shipped pin stays on 7.0.15, and
+  `scotch-7.0.18-bgraph-bipart-gg-determinism.patch` (identical to the 7.0.17
+  one) is offered as a confirmed-only behavioral patch when building 7.0.18
+  explicitly; with it the gate passes (3 x 30 runs). No public C function
+  was added or removed since 7.0.15.
+
 ## [7.0.7] - 2026-10-14
 
 ### Added
